                <head>278. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>President Eisenhower and Prime Minister Macmillan, accompanied by members of
                    their parties, were guests at a dinner on March 22 given by the Governor of
                    Bermuda, Sir John Woodall, at his residence. (Eisenhower Library, President’s
                    Appointment Book)</p>
            </div>
